# Secrets — never commit
.env
supabase.txt
# Streamlit's conventional secrets file. Nothing uses it today (config
# comes from .env via app/database.py), but it's the first place someone
# would put a credential, so it's ignored before that can happen.
.streamlit/secrets.toml
# Personal Claude Code permission grants. The ".local." in the name means
# "not shared" — but it was committed in 324551d and rode along until
# 2026-08-13, so anyone cloning inherited the allow rules on their own
# machine. Project-wide settings, if we ever want any, go in the sibling
# .claude/settings.json, which IS meant to be committed.
.claude/settings.local.json

